      "writtenOn": "2025-06-09T20:29:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I should add; I had a version that copied all the generated code for JS-\u003eC++ interop for `EventTarget` into `src/dawn/node/interop/EventTarget.cpp` (not to be confused with `src/dawn/node/bindings/EventTarget.cpp`). It worked but it was kind of ugly because the JS-\u003eC++ code for `EventTarget` relies all on the various types of inputs to the methods of `EventTarget` which are also generated by the templates. For example `EventListener`, `AddEventListenerOptions`, `EventListenerOptions`, `EventListenerInterface`, `EventListenerCallback` etc. Rather than copy all of those implementations out of the generated code I just forward declared them. But, it seemed brittle. If the definition changes (admittedly unlikely) then the forward declarations need to change. It seemed better to keep as much of the generated code as possible since it was more flexible to be able to regenerate it.",
      "revId": "1d7c16a40cf508cc09a49a3901d7bbe321e7e6c3",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
